AIM:
To analyze soccer player data using Pandas and visualize the distribution of players based on their positions.

ALGORITHM:
1. Import Pandas and Matplotlib.
2. Create a dataset of soccer players.
3. Store the data in a CSV file.
4. Read the CSV file into a DataFrame.
5. Find the top five players based on goals and salaries.
6. Calculate average player age.
7. Display players above average age.
8. Visualize player positions using a bar chart.

CODE:
import pandas as pd
import matplotlib.pyplot as plt

df = pd.DataFrame({
    "Name": ["A","B","C","D","E","F"],
    "Age": [22,25,28,30,24,35],
    "Position": ["Forward","Midfielder","Defender",
                 "Forward","Defender","Goalkeeper"],
    "Goals": [20,10,5,25,8,2],
    "Salary": [5000,4000,3000,6000,3500,2500]
})

df.to_csv("players.csv", index=False)
df = pd.read_csv("players.csv")

print("Top 5 Goals:")
print(df.nlargest(5,"Goals")[["Name","Goals"]])

print("Top 5 Salaries:")
print(df.nlargest(5,"Salary")[["Name","Salary"]])

avg = df["Age"].mean()
print("Average Age:", avg)

print("Above Average Age:")
print(df[df["Age"] > avg]["Name"])

df["Position"].value_counts().plot(kind="bar")
plt.xlabel("Position")
plt.ylabel("Number of Players")
plt.title("Players by Position")
plt.show()

